// Most case mappings are a constant delta over a run of code points, and many
// of those runs alternate upper and lower on consecutive code points. A row
// therefore carries a step: step one covers a solid run, step two covers the
// alternating Latin Extended-A pattern where each uppercase letter is
// immediately followed by its lowercase partner.

    rows ;

